// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§10", "§12.5", "§15.1", "§18.1"]

// W5-06 U5, S-911, S-313 (spec §18.1: the E0903 of the lowering is on "循環の中の手で書いた呼び出しのうちソースの順で最初のもの"; the order of the files is the one of the diagnostics, the path of the file in its package). The
// two files of each cycle are `x.onsa` and the file `x/m.onsa` of the module under it: the path `x.onsa` sorts before `x/m.onsa`, and the order the files are read in is the other. `x` has the generic function and `x.m` the
// `impl`, so the first call is the `T.default()` in `x.onsa`; `y` has the `impl` and `y.m` the generic function, so the first call is the call of `mk` in `y.onsa`. No call in `x/m.onsa` and `y/m.onsa` has a marker. `onsa check` has no
// diagnostic in the package (no name closes a cycle).

@export
pub fn anchor() -> U32 {
  1
}
